+# Workboard Table Column UX — Prioritized Implementation Roadmap
+
+Synthesis of five per-dimension audits (column sizing, data display/readability, inline
+editing, filtering/search/grouping, selection/bulk processing) into one sequenced plan.
+Verified against source: `packages/ui/src/components/table.tsx` (the `<Table>` wrapper
+hardcodes `overflow-x-auto` and forwards className to the inner `w-full` `<table>`),
+`WorkboardTable.tsx` (the `columnStyle`/`cellStyle` flex model lines 530-549, the
+`max-h-[75vh] overflow-auto` scroll container line 747, the `flex w-full` header / `width:100%`
+body rows), and the 8 `ColumnId`s in `filter-state.ts`.
+
+## Sequencing logic
+
+The headline ask — **resizable columns (drag to extend/minimise)** — leads at rank 1 even
+though it is L-effort, because it is the explicit centerpiece AND it forces the structural
+layout change (drop the `<Table>` wrapper, render `<table>` directly in the scroll container,
+move to CSS-variable widths) that several later items depend on. Rank 2 is the genuine
+correctness P0 (bulk actions mutating filtered-out rows — a silent data-mutation bug). Rank 3
+is a cheap P0 that restores the basic "this cell is editable" signal. After the P0s, items are
+ordered P1→P3 and within a tier by impact/effort, with explicit dependencies called out.
+
+Cross-audit conflict resolved: **column widths persist table-locally** (per-column
+`localStorage`, NOT in `WorkboardFilterState`, which is documented ephemeral view state),
+while **filter/search/group/column-visibility state persists to the URL** (TanStack Router).
+These are two separate persistence layers by design; do not merge them.
+
+---
+
+## Ranked roadmap
+
+### Rank 1 — Resizable columns (CENTERPIECE) · P0 · Column sizing · L · high
+The headline feature. Today every width is hardcoded in `COLUMN_SPECS` and applied through the
+flex `columnStyle`/`cellStyle`; there is no width state, no handle, no persistence. Implement a
+table-local `useColumnWidths` hook driving per-column CSS variables, header-border drag handles
+(pointer + keyboard + double-click autofit), min/max clamps, per-column `localStorage`, and a
+reset. Forces the layout move below. **Full design in the spec section.**
+Files: `apps/platform-web/src/boards/workboard/table/WorkboardTable.tsx`,
+`apps/platform-web/src/boards/workboard/toolbar/WorkboardToolbar.tsx`,
+`apps/platform-web/src/boards/workboard/WorkboardScreen.tsx`,
+`packages/ui/src/components/table.tsx` (reference only — do not edit the shared primitive).
+
+### Rank 2 — Bulk actions silently mutate filtered-out rows · P0 · Selection · M · high
+Selection persists across filter changes, but the toolbar shows raw `selection.size` and
+`handleBulkApply` writes to `[...filterState.selection]`. Select 5 → filter hides 3 → toolbar
+says "5 selected", header reads all-selected, "Set phase" mutates 3 invisible rows. Make the
+**visible** set the single source of truth for both count and bulk target: prune `selection`
+to the rendered row ids when `rows`/`items` change, OR surface "5 selected (3 hidden)" with a
+"Select only visible" affordance and scope writes to visible ids. Decide which (product call).
+Files: `WorkboardScreen.tsx`, `WorkboardTable.tsx`, `toolbar/WorkboardToolbar.tsx`.
+
+### Rank 3 — Editable cells look identical to read-only (ghost chevron killed) · P0 · Inline editing · S · high
+`INLINE_SELECT_CLASS = "[&>svg]:hidden"` (`display:none`) overrides `select.tsx`'s opacity-based
+ghost chevron, so it NEVER appears — even on hover/focus. Editable Type/Phase/Priority/Owner
+cells are byte-identical to read-only badges; zero affordance on touch. Reveal the chevron on
+row hover/focus (`group-hover:[&>svg]:inline group-focus-within:[&>svg]:inline`) instead of
+killing it. Cheap, high-impact discoverability fix.
+Files: `WorkboardTable.tsx`, `packages/ui/src/components/select.tsx`.
+
+### Rank 4 — Surface save/bulk failures with toasts + restore focus · P1 · Inline editing + Selection · M · high
+Merges three findings. `commitPatch` does `.catch(() => undefined)` and `handleBulkApply` uses
+empty `catch {}` then clears selection unconditionally — failed inline edits silently revert and
+failed bulk rows are lost. The `sonner` primitive exists but no `<Toaster/>` is mounted.
+**Shared prerequisite: mount `<Toaster/>` once in `WorkboardScreen`.** Then: toast on inline
+rejection + `aria-live`; in bulk, collect failed ids, keep them selected, toast "Updated 47 of
+50 — 3 failed. Retry?", only clear succeeded ids; and on selection→0, move focus to the
+select-all header checkbox (today focus drops to `<body>` when the bulk fieldset unmounts).
+Files: `WorkboardScreen.tsx`, `WorkboardTable.tsx`, `toolbar/WorkboardToolbar.tsx`,
+`apps/platform-web/src/data/work-items/use-work-items.ts`, `packages/ui/src/components/sonner.tsx`.
+
+### Rank 5 — Tags inline cell clips its own input/chips · P1 · Inline editing + Data display · M · medium
+Same defect flagged by two audits. `TagInput` forced to `flex-nowrap overflow-hidden` in a
+~10rem cell squeezes the `flex-1` input toward zero and clips extra chips with no `+N`. Render a
+compact `TagList`-style summary with a `+N` counter at rest, expanding to the full `TagInput`
+on focus/click (mirrors the read-only `TagList max={3}` path that is already better).
+Files: `WorkboardTable.tsx`, `packages/ui/src/components/tag-input.tsx`.
+
+### Rank 6 — Badge color system: Priority/Phase ramps + family differentiation · P1 · Data display · M · high
+Merges three findings. In dark mode `bg-accent`/`bg-secondary`/`bg-muted` are all neutral
+(chroma 0, ~0.09 L apart) so High/Med/Low and Plan/Execute/Review collapse to near-identical
+grays; `bg-muted` is simultaneously Type, Priority-low, Phase-plan, Health-on_track and the
+Archived chip, killing cross-column scannability; and the loudest badge is `done` (least
+actionable). Give Priority and Phase dedicated chroma-bearing token ramps that survive both
+themes (or interim: a colored leading dot on every level); render Type as an outlined category
+tag so "category" reads distinct from filled "status" badges; invert weight so `execute` is
+emphasized and `done` is quiet.
+Files: `packages/ui/src/components/priority-badge.tsx`, `phase-pill.tsx`,
+`work-item-type-badge.tsx`, `health-badge.tsx`, `packages/ui/src/styles/tokens.css`.
+
+### Rank 7 — Shift-click range selection + larger hit target · P1 · Selection · M · high
+Selecting N rows = N clicks; the only target is a 16px checkbox and the rest of the row is inert.
+Track the last-toggled flattened index in a ref; on shift-click select the inclusive range over
+`flatRows` order (skipping group headers); update the anchor on plain clicks. Enlarge the click
+area to the whole leading selection cell.
+Files: `WorkboardTable.tsx`.
+
+### Rank 8 — Persist filter/search/group/column state + saved views · P1 · Filtering · L · high
+The entire `WorkboardFilterState` lives in plain `useState`; a reload or a hop to the Graph
+sub-board route drops all facets, search, grouping and column visibility, and there is no way to
+name/share a view. Serialize to URL search params via TanStack Router (sets as comma lists,
+default-equal facets omitted) so views are reload-safe, back-button-able and shareable; layer
+named quick-view chips ("My open", "This week") on that substrate. Minimum first step:
+`localStorage` keyed by board. (Kept separate from rank-1 width persistence by design.)
+Files: `WorkboardScreen.tsx`, `filter-state.ts`.
+
+### Rank 9 — Searchable Owner/Department facets · P1 · Filtering · M · high
+`FacetFilterMenu` renders every option as a scroll-only checkbox; Owner/Department grow with the
+workspace with no type-to-find. Add an optional `searchable` prop (auto when `options.length > ~8`)
+that renders a `cmdk` Command input + filtered list (cmdk already ships in `CommandPalette.tsx`).
+Files: `toolbar/FacetFilterMenu.tsx`, `toolbar/WorkboardToolbar.tsx`.
+
+### Rank 10 — Expose selection as a grid to assistive tech · P1/P2 · Selection · S · medium
+Container is `role="table"` while rows carry `aria-selected`/`data-state="selected"` — a plain
+table is not a selection container, so selection isn't announced. Promote to `role="grid"` +
+`aria-multiselectable="true"`, switch cell `role="cell"`→`"gridcell"` (also resolves the
+JSDoc/code drift the inline-editing audit flagged), and mount one persistent `sr-only`
+`aria-live` region for the selected count (today's count lives inside the conditionally-mounted
+bulk fieldset and announces unreliably). **Couple with rank 15** — grid role sets the keyboard
+expectation roving nav fulfills.
+Files: `WorkboardTable.tsx`, `toolbar/WorkboardToolbar.tsx`.
+
+### Rank 11 — Wire (or delete) the "/" search shortcut · P1 · Filtering · S · medium · QUICK WIN
+A `<kbd>/</kbd>` badge promises focus-search but no handler exists (`ShellLayout` only binds
+Cmd/Ctrl+K and 1-5 and early-returns inside inputs). Add a window keydown listener that focuses
+the search input on `/` when focus is not in a field — or delete the badge.
+Files: `toolbar/WorkboardToolbar.tsx`, `apps/platform-web/src/shell/ShellLayout.tsx`.
+
+### Rank 12 — Unify Clear-filters scope + count search · P2 · Filtering · S · medium · QUICK WIN
+Two "Clear filters" controls behave differently (toolbar keeps `search`, empty-state clears it),
+and `activeFilterCount` ignores search so a search-only empty board shows no Clear button. Make
+the toolbar Clear reset search too, and include trimmed search in `activeFilterCount`.
+Files: `toolbar/WorkboardToolbar.tsx`, `WorkboardScreen.tsx`.
+
+### Rank 13 — Row-state differentiation (selected vs hover vs group vs archived) · P2 · Data display + Selection · M · medium
+Selected (`bg-muted`), hover (`bg-muted/50`) and group header (`bg-muted/40`) are the same hue
+differing only in opacity — and hovering a selected row lightens it. Archived rows use blanket
+`opacity-60` over already-muted text, dimming status badges too. Give selection a distinct cue
+(leading accent bar + `bg-primary/10`, `data-[state=selected]:hover:bg-primary/15` so selected
+wins over hover); strengthen the swimlane band (full-opacity `bg-muted` + `border-y`); replace
+archived opacity with a muted token + a non-contrast cue (left rail / strikethrough title)
+keeping badges at full opacity.
+Files: `packages/ui/src/components/table.tsx`, `WorkboardTable.tsx`.
+
+### Rank 14 — Sticky + collapsible swimlane headers + per-swimlane select-all · P2 · Data display + Selection + Grouping · L · medium
+**Depends on rank 1** (the swimlane row must already carry `var(--table-width)`). Group rows are
+ordinary virtualized rows: not sticky, not collapsible, no checkbox, label starts at x=0. Make
+the active group header `position:sticky; top:<header-height>` (react-virtual sticky-active
+pattern), add a collapse toggle that drops the bucket from `flatRows`, add a tri-state checkbox
+that selects exactly that bucket, surface group counts, and indent the label to the Name column.
+Files: `WorkboardTable.tsx`, `toolbar/WorkboardToolbar.tsx`.
+
+### Rank 15 — Grid keyboard navigation (roving tabindex) · P2 · Inline editing + Selection · L · medium
+Merges two findings. ~9 tab stops per editable row, no roving tabindex, no Space-to-toggle,
+no Cmd/Ctrl+A, no Escape-to-clear. Add roving-tabindex cell nav: one Tab stop per cell, Arrow
+keys between cells, Enter/Space to enter the inline control, Escape to return to the cell /
+clear selection, Shift+Arrow to extend a range, Cmd/Ctrl+A to select visible. Minimum viable:
+defer each inline control's tabindex until its cell is focused, and wire Escape to clear.
+**Couple with rank 10.**
+Files: `WorkboardTable.tsx`, `toolbar/WorkboardToolbar.tsx`.
+
+### Rank 16 — Expand the bulk-action cluster · P2 · Selection · M · medium
+The cluster only offers Set phase / Set priority, yet the two most common batch ops — reassign
+Owner and Archive/Unarchive — are missing. Route bulk Owner (AssigneePicker menu),
+Archive/Unarchive and optionally Type through the existing `onBulkApply(patch)` seam (already
+accepts an arbitrary `WorkItemPatch`; no new plumbing).
+Files: `toolbar/WorkboardToolbar.tsx`, `WorkboardScreen.tsx`.
+
+### Rank 17 — Touch / no-hover affordances · P2 · Inline editing · S · medium
+Copy-title, row Actions and tag-remove are all `opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100`; on coarse
+pointers there is no hover and `:focus-visible` rarely fires from touch, so they are unusable.
+Gate the hover-reveal behind `@media (hover:hover)` and keep controls visible at reduced opacity
+on coarse pointers. Apply uniformly.
+Files: `WorkboardTable.tsx`, `packages/ui/src/components/tag-input.tsx`.
+
+### Rank 18 — Broaden search scope + scoped placeholder + debounce · P2 · Filtering · M · medium
+`searchMatches` tests only title + tags, so owner/department/type queries return an unexplained
+empty board. Broaden it to owner name, department and type label (resolve owner id via the
+owners list); set a scoped placeholder; feed the term through `useDeferredValue`; and fix the
+WebKit `::-webkit-search-cancel-button` overlapping the badge.
+Files: `filter-state.ts`, `toolbar/WorkboardToolbar.tsx`, `WorkboardScreen.tsx`.
+
+### Rank 19 — Filter legibility + toolbar declutter · P2 · Filtering · M · medium
+Facet triggers show a count but not which values are active; no removable chips; no per-facet
+Select-all/Clear or option counts; the single flex-wrap row of ~10 controls reflows. Render a
+removable filter-chip row beneath the toolbar, add Select-all/Clear + per-option counts inside
+each facet, and consolidate the 5 facet buttons + the decorative `FilterIcon` into one "Filter"
+popover showing a total active count.
+Files: `toolbar/WorkboardToolbar.tsx`, `toolbar/FacetFilterMenu.tsx`, `WorkboardScreen.tsx`.
+
+### Rank 20 — Readability & feedback polish bundle · P3 · Mixed · S · low
+Low-effort, low-risk cleanups: Due left-align (or move to last data column) to kill the interior
+whitespace river; drop the redundant Source tooltip (chip already shows the label); read-only
+Owner `block truncate` + avatar parity with the editable picker; in-flight pending cell
+treatment during optimistic save; duplicate/blank tag-add feedback; `aria-invalid` on rejected
+inline selects; unify the ghost editable-cell hover token; relabel Group "none" → "No grouping".
+Files: `WorkboardTable.tsx`, `provenance-chip.tsx`, `tag-input.tsx`, `select.tsx`,
+`toolbar/WorkboardToolbar.tsx`, `filter-state.ts`, `assignee-picker.tsx`, `use-work-items.ts`.
+
+---
+
+## Resizable columns — concrete spec
+
+**Approach.** Resize cannot be bolted on. Two blockers: (a) the shared `<Table>` primitive wraps
+`<table>` in a hardcoded `relative w-full overflow-x-auto` div and forwards className to the
+inner `w-full` table, so under row virtualization (wrapper height = `getTotalSize()`, thousands
+of px) the horizontal scrollbar is parked off-screen and unreachable; (b) the `flex w-full` /
+row `width:100%` model can express neither fixed dragged widths nor horizontal overflow. Fix
+both **in `WorkboardTable` only** (the sole consumer of the primitive): stop using `<Table>` and
+render `<table className="w-max …" style={{minWidth:"100%"}}>` directly inside the existing
+`scrollRef` (`max-h-[75vh] overflow-auto`) so ONE fixed-height container scrolls both axes and
+the sticky header stays pinned. Convert the 8 data `ColumnSpec`s from rem to px and drive each
+width from a CSS custom property; mutate the variable imperatively during drag and commit to
+React state + `localStorage` only on pointer-up. Mirror the already-installed
+`@tanstack/react-table` CSS-variable column-sizing pattern without adopting the headless table.
+Selection (2.5rem) and Actions (3rem) columns stay fixed with no handle.
+
+**Components to touch.** `WorkboardTable.tsx` (layout swap, `columnStyle` rewrite, handles,
+autofit refs); new colocated hook `table/useColumnWidths.ts`; `WorkboardToolbar.tsx` (global
+"Reset column widths" item in the Columns dropdown); `WorkboardScreen.tsx` (thread one
+`onResetColumnWidths` prop Screen→Toolbar; do NOT lift the width map); `table.tsx` and
+`filter-state.ts` as read-only references (no edits). Extend `WorkboardTable.test.tsx`.
+
+**Per-column width state.** Table-local `useColumnWidths(columns)` returns
+`{ widths: Record<ColumnId, number>, tableWidth, onPointerResizeStart, onKeyResize, autofit,
+reset }`. `widths` are px seeded from each spec's new px default; each `ColumnSpec` gains
+`minWidthPx` (default 64) and `maxWidthPx` (default 720). `tableWidth = SELECT + Σ(visible data
+widths) + (showActions ? ACTIONS : 0)`. Width is NOT added to `WorkboardFilterState` (documented
+ephemeral view state). Widths and `--table-width` are published as CSS variables on the scroll
+container; data cells become `flex:0 0 var(--col-<id>)`; Name/Tags drop `flex-grow`.
+
+**Persistence.** `localStorage`, keyed per column: `workboard.table.colw.v1.<columnId>`. Read on
+mount under `typeof window !== "undefined"` + try/catch; ignore `NaN` and unknown ids so adding/
+removing a `ColumnId` can never corrupt stored state. Hidden columns keep their stored width
+(orthogonal to visibility). Written only on pointer-up / keyboard-commit / autofit. `reset()`
+clears the per-column keys and restores defaults. Separate from the rank-8 URL filter layer.
+
+**Drag-handle UX.** Each resizable `<TableHead>` is `position:relative` with a focusable handle
+as its last child: `<span role="separator" aria-orientation="vertical" aria-label="Resize {col}
+column" aria-valuemin/max/now tabIndex={0}>`, a 6-8px hit area straddling the right border via
+`translate-x-1/2`, transparent → `hover:bg-border` → `data-[dragging]:bg-ring` /
+`focus-visible:bg-ring`, `cursor-col-resize`, `touch-none select-none`. PointerDown: setPointer
+Capture, record startX/startWidth, set `document.body` cursor/userSelect. PointerMove
+(rAF-throttled): `clamp(startWidth + dx, min, max)` → `container.style.setProperty('--col-<id>',
+…)` + recompute `--table-width`; NO setState. PointerUp: read final var, commit to state +
+`localStorage`, clear body styles. Keyboard: Arrow ±16 (Shift ±64), Home=min, End=max,
+Enter/Space/double-click = **autofit** (max `scrollWidth` over a ref-callback `Map` of mounted
+cell nodes + padding, clamped — honest best-effort fit-to-visible under virtualization). Global
+reset in the Columns dropdown.
+
+**Edge cases.**
+- *Virtualizer:* width is a CSS variable, never virtualizer input; no `measure()` on resize (row
+  height unchanged); rAF-batched var writes + state-on-pointerup-only mean mounted cells never
+  re-render mid-drag (driving width from state would re-render every virtual cell per mousemove).
+- *Sticky header:* header now lives in the SAME single scroll container as the body, so it
+  scrolls horizontally in lock-step and stays pinned vertically (`sticky top-0 z-10`); the header
+  row carries `var(--table-width)` so its bottom hairline spans the scrolled width.
+- *Grow columns:* Name/Tags lose `flex-grow` (grow makes dragging meaningless — freed space just
+  reflows); every data cell becomes `flex:0 0 var(--col-<id>)`.
+- *Min widths / overflow:* clamp each resize to `[minWidthPx, maxWidthPx]`; add
+  `overflow-hidden text-ellipsis` to ALL data cells so a shrunk column truncates inside its box
+  instead of spilling into its neighbor.
+- *Horizontal-scrollbar trap:* must NOT reuse the shared `<Table>` wrapper (its `overflow-x-auto`
+  under virtualization makes the x-scrollbar unreachable).
+- *Fill-when-narrow:* `minWidth:100%` on the `<table>` so it fills the viewport when summed widths
+  are smaller and scrolls when they exceed it (no ragged right gap); the swimlane group row also
+  takes `var(--table-width)` so its `bg-muted/40` spans the full scrolled width.
+
+**Build steps (ordered).**
+1. Add px defaults + `minWidthPx`/`maxWidthPx` to the 8 `ColumnSpec`s (rem→px so all sizing is
+   one unit).
+2. Build `useColumnWidths` (state seeded from defaults; per-column `localStorage` read/write with
+   `typeof window` + try/catch + NaN/unknown-id guards; `clamp`, `autofit`, `reset`).
+3. Replace the `<Table>` wrapper with a direct `<table className="w-max" minWidth:100%>` inside
+   `scrollRef`, keeping TableHeader/Body/Row/Head/Cell; publish `--table-width` and `--col-*` on
+   the scroll container.
+4. Rewrite `columnStyle` data path to `flex:0 0 var(--col-<id>)`, drop grow; set header row, body
+   `offsetStyle`, and swimlane row to `width:var(--table-width)`; add `overflow-hidden
+   text-ellipsis` to data cells.
+5. Add the `role="separator"` handle to each resizable head with pointer + keyboard + dblclick
+   handlers wired to the hook; set body cursor/userSelect during an active drag.
+6. Add the autofit ref-callback `Map` of mounted cell content nodes; implement fit-to-visible.
+7. Add "Reset column widths" (`DropdownMenuSeparator` + item) to the Columns dropdown, threaded
+   via one `onResetColumnWidths` prop Screen→Toolbar; keep the width map in the table hook.
+8. Extend `WorkboardTable.test.tsx`: handle renders `role="separator"` + `aria-valuenow`;
+   ArrowRight increases width and persists to the `localStorage` key; `reset()` restores default;
+   min clamp holds (assert committed state/vars — jsdom has no layout). Keep existing
+   colcount/header-order tests green (handles are not `columnheader`s).
+
+---
+
+## Quick wins (S-effort, visible, independent of the resize refactor)
+- **Reveal the ghost chevron** on row hover/focus (rank 3) — restores the editable-cell signal.
+- **Wire or delete the "/" search hint** (rank 11) — stop promising behavior that doesn't exist.
+- **Unify Clear-filters + count search** in `activeFilterCount` (rank 12).
+- **`overflow-hidden text-ellipsis`** on fixed data cells — stops Owner/Type names spilling into
+  the next column today (also a prerequisite for shrinking under resize).
+- **Drop the redundant Source tooltip**; **left-align Due** (rank 20).
+- **Relabel Group "none" → "No grouping"** (rank 20).
+- **Persistent `sr-only` live region** for the selected count (part of rank 10).
+
+## Risks
+- **Test regressions:** existing colcount / header-order / explicit-ARIA tests in
+  `WorkboardTable.test.tsx` will break from the layout swap and the `role="grid"`/`gridcell`
+  change — resize handles must NOT be counted as `columnheader`s; update assertions deliberately.
+- **Virtualizer jank:** if column width ever flows through React state instead of the CSS
+  variable, every mounted virtual cell re-renders per mousemove. Keep drag writes imperative;
+  setState only on pointer-up.
+- **Selection-semantics change:** the rank-2 fix alters the current cross-filter persistence
+  behavior — explicitly choose prune-to-visible vs. surface "N hidden". This is a product call,
+  not just a code fix.
+- **`localStorage` column-set drift:** ignore `NaN`/unknown ids on read so adding/removing a
+  `ColumnId` in `COLUMN_IDS` can never corrupt stored widths.
+- **Forking from the shared primitive:** rendering `<table>` directly (rather than editing
+  `table.tsx`) is a deliberate blast-radius mitigation, but WorkboardTable then diverges from the
+  `<Table>` component — track drift if the primitive evolves.
+- **Coupling:** rank 10 (grid role) and rank 15 (roving keyboard nav) must ship together — a grid
+  role implies arrow-key navigation; one without the other breaks the AT contract. Rank 14
+  depends on rank 1's `var(--table-width)` swimlane row.
+- **Shared `<Toaster/>` prerequisite:** rank 4's inline-rollback and bulk-failure toasts both
+  no-op until a single `<Toaster/>` is mounted in `WorkboardScreen`.
+- **URL persistence interactions:** rank 8 serialization must omit default-equal facets and
+  coexist with selection persistence and the separate Graph route.
